rs6000: accept -mp32 and -mp64 on the PS3 targets

PS3 makefiles select the data model with -mp32 (32-bit pointers, the
default) and -mp64.  Make them aliases of -mno-lp64 and -mlp64.

--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/ps3-lp64.opt
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/ps3-lp64.opt
@@ -26,3 +26,11 @@
 mlp64
 Target Mask(LP64) Var(rs6000_isa_flags)
 Use LP64 data model (64-bit pointers and longs).
+
+mp32
+Target RejectNegative Alias(mlp64) NegativeAlias
+Use the ILP32 data model (32-bit pointers); the default.  Same as -mno-lp64.
+
+mp64
+Target RejectNegative Alias(mlp64)
+Use the LP64 data model (64-bit pointers).  Same as -mlp64.
